  "security_implications": "The chunk controls the initial state added at the start of AES operations. If add_state_in_sel is corrupted or mis-selected, add_state_in may become zero instead of the required transposed IV, causing a wrong cipher result. This could break data confidentiality/integrity (ciphertext is incorrect) but does not directly expose secret keys. The default zero assignment acts as a safety net against unknown select values, preventing garbage propagation, but verifying the exclusivity of the enum is important to avoid unintended silent zeroes.",
